Subject: Port: online play between the releases, by the draft's simulation profile
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3

The original keeps the releases apart online: GetNetworkVersionWord makes
its word of the region and build number, and matchmaking (the AP key and
its filter), the socket's packets and friends' status all compare it. The
port only plays other PCs, so its games of every release now speak one
protocol online instead, MSCHARGED_ONLINE_VERSION_WORD
(include/mscharged_online_releases.h), which no original word can be, so no
Wii meets a PC. LAN keeps the original word.

Machines of different releases then have to simulate by the same rules
(tweak patch 0057). Each machine's draft entry (NetworkDraftMachineInfo,
which every machine sends its host in matchmaking and friend matches) now
carries its own simulation profile; the host picks the match's profile with
mscharged_sim_resolve (their own one when all share it, else the European
revision 2's) and sends it with the draft (NetMessageDraft), and every
machine, the host too, takes it when the draft arrives, long before the
match loads and its rollback starts. Leaving online or LAN play puts the
module's own profile back.

